</p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://www.bbc.co.uk/go/rss/int/news/-/news/uk-12345809 target=_self >London bomber given &#39;Pakistan advice&#39;</a><br/>The 7/7 ringleader received guidance in phone calls from Pakistan in the days before the bombings, the inquests have been told.</p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://www.bbc.co.uk/go/rss/int/news/-/news/world-europe-12347525 target=_self >Scandinavian sea tunnel planned</a><br/>Denmark is to build a sea tunnel to Germany, cutting road and rail journey times between western Europe and Scandinavia.</p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://www.bbc.co.uk/go/rss/int/news/-/news/world-europe-12350202 target=_self >New broker for deadlocked Belgium</a><br/>King Albert II of Belgium picks a new mediator in a bid to end the deadlock over forming a government for the divided country.</p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://www.bbc.co.uk/go/rss/int/news/-/news/world-europe-12344261 target=_self >EU wants more air passenger data</a><br/>The EU plans to expand transfers of air passenger data in a drive to prevent terrorism and other serious crimes such as drug trafficking.</p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://www.bbc.co.uk/go/rss/int/news/-/news/world-europe-12344603 target=_self >Berlin eviction prompts clashes</a><br/>More than 2,000 police face resistance from hundreds of activists in Berlin as they move in to clear a former squat.</p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://www.bbc.co.uk/go/rss/int/news/-/news/uk-politics-12338921 target=_self >Ex-minister denies regime change plan</a><br/>Former UK Foreign Secretary Jack Straw insists regime change in Iraq was never UK policy, as the Iraq inquiry public hearings end.</p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://www.bbc.co.uk/go/rss/int/news/-/news/world-europe-12348673 target=_self >Four shot dead in North Caucasus</a><br/>Four traffic policemen are shot dead by masked men in the Russian North Caucasus republic of Kabardino-Balkaria, reports say.</p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://www.bbc.co.uk/go/rss/int/news/-/news/world-europe-12343190 target=_self >Moscow bombing deaths rise to 36</a><br/>A 36th victim has died of injuries sustained in the Domodedovo airport bomb attack near Moscow, Russian officials say.</p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://www.bbc.co.uk/go/rss/int/news/-/news/world-latin-america-12342862 target=_self >Duvalier: frozen Swiss funds not mine</a><br/>Haiti&#39;s ex-leader Jean-Claude Duvalier says millions of dollars frozen in Swiss bank accounts are not his and should go to rebuild Haiti.</p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://www.bbc.co.uk/go/rss/int/news/-/news/entertainment-arts-12344572 target=_self >Allen movie to open Cannes gala</a><br/>Director Woody Allen&#39;s romantic comedy Midnight in Paris is to open the Cannes Film Festival in May, organisers announce.</p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://www.bbc.co.uk/go/rss/int/news/-/news/world-europe-12345063 target=_self >Berlusconi belly dancer Ruby &#39;to marry&#39;</a><br/>The teenage dancer at the heart of a scandal involving Italian PM Silvio Berlusconi tells a paper she plans to get married.</p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://www.bbc.co.uk/go/rss/int/news/-/news/uk-12336061 target=_self >UK perfume ad banned for &#39;drug simulation&#39;</a><br/>An advert for an Yves Saint Laurent perfume is banned by the Advertising Standards Authority for appearing to show a woman simulating drug use.</p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://www.bbc.co.uk/go/rss/int/news/-/news/business-12352811 target=_self >Unilever profits in strong rise</a><br/>Unilever, the maker of Knorr soups, Cif cleaning products and Ben and Jerry&#39;s ice cream saw an 18% jump in annual profits.</p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://www.bbc.co.uk/go/rss/int/news/-/news/business-12342467 target=_self >Spain&#39;s BBVA posts 